{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017hDaW7dfoiWWTetnJvVCTo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system John Liechty runs for himself. Grounded claims from the project docs:\n\n- **It's a single-folder, plain-markdown task manager.** Everything lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no OneDrive, no syncing, no database). Markdown files are the source of truth: `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, per-domain files (`domains/academic.md`, `commercial.md`, `family.md`, `writing.md`), plus archives (`CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`). Tasks move through a lifecycle: Active â†’ Done / Cancelled / Saved-for-Later / Restored.\n\n- **It ships as a local web app, not a hosted service.** `anchor_gui.py` is a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders the dashboard and writes directly to the markdown. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`. `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror that also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It has grown a substantial \"R&D control surface\" for trio-driven development.** Beyond tasks, each project gets a window that orchestrates a three-skill pipeline â€” **researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build)** â€” as durable, isolated, server-side sessions. This surface has shipped through four versioned iterations (v2 sessions/summaries/grass â†’ v3 \"Mission Control\" â†’ v4 \"Project Cockpit,\" all merged to master).\n\n- **The R&D cockpit's concrete capabilities:** real ConPTY interactive terminals (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE transport), per-session git-worktree isolation, cached + grounding-validated session/project summaries, lane status lights (green/amber/red/grey), an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), a cost/tokens/time rollup, a \"Grass Catchers\" idea board, and type-aware deliverable launching (skill/tool/service/program/doc).\n\n- **It's deliberately dependency-light.** Python 3.8+ stdlib only, with exactly **one declared exception** â€” optional `pywinpty` for the terminal subsystem (lazy import, degrades gracefully). `distro.py` enforces this with an import scan.\n\n- **It self-tests daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file, exercising every endpoint, and walking the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, no touching the `:8777` service), then writing a dated report to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **Branding/identity:** presented as a Ghost World Labs tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" for a single user (J.C. Liechty) spanning academic, commercial, family, and writing domains."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"198c03af-01f2-4f4c-b520-e4d602e6833e","uuid":"5f4f261e-8ca5-413f-aab0-a8e34fc4d920","request_id":"req_011Cc1iDkwkX643NaRRqpzuB"}
